Hardware Awareness

Before executing any task, Chameha requests a hardware profile from the Hardware Abstraction Layer (HAL).

This enables intelligent decisions such as:

selecting the appropriate AI model
respecting memory limits
monitoring battery level
reducing workload during thermal events
selecting CPU, GPU or NPU execution
adapting to mobile and desktop devices automatically
Remote Device Control

Remote operations are executed through AION using capability-based permissions.

Supported operations include:

open applications
launch workflows
file management
notification delivery
screen control
power management
clipboard synchronization
desktop automation
mobile automation

Every privileged action requires permission through the Capability Broker.

